Assignment: Pass a Student's Name Between React Components

Objective: Learn how to pass data from one React component to another using props.

Requirements:

Create two React components: NameInput and NameDisplay.

In the NameInput component, create a text input field where the user can enter their name.

Create a button labeled Submit.

When the user enters their name and clicks Submit, pass the name to the NameDisplay component using props.

The NameDisplay component should display the entered name.

Expected Output:

When the user enters Adhnan and clicks Submit, the page should display:

Hello, Adhnan!

Conditions:

Use React functional components.

Use the useState hook to store the input.

Pass the name from one component to another using props.

Keep the input and display logic in separate components.